    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40030": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist III",
      "description": "Department: Financial Aid and Scholarships\nAdministrative Specialist III | Working Title | Administrative Specialist III | Position # | A01027 | Department | Financial Aid and Scholarships\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Administrative Specialist III Working Title Administrative Specialist III Position # A01027 Department Financial Aid and Scholarships Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: $30,000.00 Closing: 11/6/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Administrative Specialist III is responsible for providing departmental staff support, responding to inquiries from students, staff or external partners. In addition to supporting departmental outreach and engagement efforts. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Duties & Responsibilities: Performs secretarial and clerical duties associated with the Financial Aid office, including acknowledging and greeting all students and visitors, answering a multi-line telephone, managing and directing students and phone traffic. Maintains the security and confidentiality of all records in accordance with FERPA. Monitors and controls the wait time of students and other visitors through the check-in system. Helping students navigate financial aid portals or complete forms. Communicating aid eligibility and verification needs with students. Assisting students in collecting documents needed for financial aid and verifications. Working with students to clear blockers if able. Responding to student inquiries and directing them to appropriate resources. Monitor the Financial Aid email account and respond to all inquiries. Perform related/other duties as required Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Working knowledge of Banner information system. • Knowledge of designated data system functions. • Knowledge of record management systems and retention policies and procedures. • Knowledge of federal laws and regulations and state directives, policies, and procedures surrounding privacy and record maintenance. • Ability to analyze, evaluate, and recommend new or revised records systems flow. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assists students, parents, staff, faculty, student loan guarantee foundations, and lenders Minimum Qualifications: The formal education equivalent of a High School Diploma E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=40025": {
      "title": "Student Development Specialist",
      "description": "Department: Recruitment\nStudent Development Specialist | Working Title | Admissions Counselor | Position # | A01300 | Department | Recruitment\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Student Development Specialist Working Title Admissions Counselor Position # A01300 Department Recruitment Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Staff # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/3/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: This position reports to the Senior Associate Director for Enrollment Outreach and supporting the Associate Director of Transfer Admissions and collaborating with the Campus Experience Coordinator, plays a pivotal role in the overall guest experience for prospective students and their families in the Welcome Center. This position coordinates the recruitment, hiring, training, scheduling, and management of student staff who serve as tour guides and ambassadors. Additionally, serving as the backup in-house admissions counselor assistant for both transfer student and first-year recruitment. This role is responsible for assisting with emails, phone calls, and in-person service for transfer students and incoming students while being primarily located in the Welcome Center. Duties & Responsibilities: Responsible for managing the day-to-day logistics, appearance, and operational readiness of key guest-facing spaces within the Welcome Center, including the Welcome Desk, Presentation Room, and other high-traffic visitor areas. Oversees the recruitment, training, and performance of student tour guides in these guest-facing spaces to ensure a welcoming, professional, and service-oriented experience for prospective students, families, and university guests. Works collaboratively to maintain exceptional presentation standards and deliver a high-quality visitor experience Responsible for overseeing the onboarding, training, and certification process for newly hired student tour guides Coordinates and tracks all required training milestones, ensuring guides successfully progress through certification requirements and are fully prepared to represent the university Serves as one of the primary points of contact for new tour guides, providing guidance, answering questions, and offering ongoing support throughout the training process Additionally, has primary oversight of continued training for all student tour guides throughout the year. Including identifying needed training areas and creating training protocols for exceptional Welcome Ambassadors Maintains accountability standards, monitors individual progress, and works proactively to address challenges, ensuring a positive training experience and a high level of preparedness, professionalism, and performance among student staff Maintain up-to-date knowledge of admissions processes and university programs to provide accurate and insightful guidance to prospective students and families Oversee and audit inventory tracking for Campus Visits storage and materials Perform all other duties as assigned to support Arkansas State University’s mission. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: · Ability to comply with University policies · Maintain regular and punctual attendance General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Some nights and weekends can be required Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor's degree and one year of relevant experience are required. A valid US Driver License with a clear driving record of at least two years is required. Two (2) years of relevant experience are preferred. Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39973": {
      "title": "Faculty 12 Mo",
      "description": "Department: College of Veterinary Medicine\nFaculty 12 Mo | Working Title | Assistant or Associate Professor of Veterinary Clinical Pathology (Half Time) | Position # | VET001 | Department | College of Veterinary Medicine\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Faculty 12 Mo Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Veterinary Clinical Pathology (Half Time) Position # VET001 Department College of Veterinary Medicine Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/14/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: Arkansas State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a 12-month, half time, non-tenure (teaching) track, Assistant or Associate Professor in Veterinary Clinical Pathology. This will be a predominantly teaching position (90% teaching, 10% service). Teaching of DVM students will be in a competency-based veterinary curriculum incorporating lecture, lab and small group learning. Service will include College, University and outside service and may include opportunities for diagnostic service. This position is designated at 0.5 full-time equivalent (FTE), representing 50% of a full-time appointment. Duties & Responsibilities: Contribute to competency-based curriculum development with a focus on veterinary clinical pathology Teach diagnostic reasoning in the DVM curriculum in classroom and laboratory settings (+/- clinical settings) Contribute to college and university committees and/or serve on regional or national professional organizations Mentor DVM students Other duties as assigned Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and staff Ability to communicate effectively across CVM stakeholders Ability to prioritize tasks, deliver results in a timely manner, and function independently General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date The search will continue until the position is filled. Those who apply by the closing date will receive priority consideration. Preferred Qualifications: · Two years’ experience as a veterinary clinical pathologist · Demonstrated ability to provide high-quality teaching at the college or university level · Ability to work in a team within an interdisciplinary environment and in collaboration with other faculty members Minimum Qualifications: · A DVM (or equivalent) and hold, or be in the process of obtaining, board certification in veterinary clinical pathology (DACVP or equivalent) · Hold or obtain a license to practice veterinary medicine in Arkansas Other job-related education and/or experience may be substituted for all or part of these basic requirements, except for certification or licensure requirements, upon approval of the qualifications review committee. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39741": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 Mo",
      "description": "Department: Theatre\nAssistant Professor 9 Mo | Working Title | Assistant Professor of Dance and Choreography 9 Mo | Position # | F00266 | Department | Theatre\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Dance and Choreography 9 Mo Position # F00266 Department Theatre Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/9/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of Theatre at Arkansas State University invites applications for a Full-Time Assistant Professor of Theatre in Dance and Choreography. This is a 9-month tenure-track teaching appointment starting Fall 2027. Duties & Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be responsible for: Teaching a 4/4 load, which typically includes three academic courses and one production course (directing/choreographing). Other possible courses include, but are not limited to, Theatre Appreciation, Ballet, Musical Theatre Dance, Jazz Dance, Tap Dance, Folk and other Dance courses as determined by the faculty member’s area(s) of specialty and expertise. Maintaining an active record of research and/or creative activity Overseeing the Stage Manager for shows when directing. Attending evening/weekend rehearsals as appropriate Mentoring and supervising student choreographers and dance captains. Being available for student supervision during evening and weekend rehearsals and performances Working collegially and collaboratively with students and faculty. Department Overview: The Arkansas State University Department of Theatre offers rigorous theatre training in a liberal arts environment. Students receive a comprehensive education, whether choosing a general approach or the more select experiences within the three emphases: Acting, Design and Technology, or Musical Theatre. The curriculum is designed to combine classroom instruction with practical production experience, as both are integral to the student’s development. Classroom experiences provide theoretical, historical, and critical examinations of the theatre as art, craft, and discipline, while production experiences offer practical opportunities for exploring and applying these concepts. This liberal arts-based education provides opportunities to master critical thinking, communication, and creative problem-solving skills, preparing graduates to become engaged, thoughtful, and compassionate citizens of a global world. Facilities: The Department of Theatre is housed within Fowler Center, Arkansas State University’s premier performing arts complex. The 344-seat Drama Theatre serves as the primary venue for plays and musicals, featuring stepped seating to maximize sight lines and acoustics designed for spoken drama productions. The proscenium features a 40’ x 20’ opening, and a complete catwalk system provides access for lighting and rigging areas. The stage house features a suspended floor and full fly-loft, rigged so that scenic properties may be “flown” out of view. Adjacent to the Drama Theatre is the Simpson Theatre, a flexible black box space that allows for various configurations, providing students opportunities to develop skills required to work in many different kinds of venues. Additional facilities include a Light Lab equipped with intelligent LED theatrical lighting and a small theatrical sound system, a Design Lab featuring Apple iMacs with CAD, lighting and sound design software, and access to Adobe’s Creative Cloud, as well as drafting tables and a wide-format printer. The Costume Shop is equipped with 14 Bernina sewing machines, industrial irons, sergers, a dye vat, cutting tables, and an embroidery machine. The Scene Shop is among the finest in the region, equipped with a variety of professional-grade stationary and portable power tools, as well as a 3D printer. About Arkansas State University: Arkansas State University (A-State), founded in 1909, is the second largest university in Arkansas and serves over 15,000 students. As a Carnegie Research 2 institution and the premier university of the mid-South, A-State is committed to teaching, research, and service. Located in Jonesboro, A-State offers a vibrant campus life with a diverse student body and a strong tradition of student-focused instruction. With more than 150 degree programs, including robust online offerings, A-State combines world-class research with academic excellence and is a catalyst for progress in the Delta and Mid-South region. About Jonesboro: Jonesboro is the regional hub of Northeast Arkansas for healthcare, entertainment, business and industry. It is the 5th largest city in Arkansas with a population of over 76,000. The Metropolitan Statistical Area (MSA) encompasses over 130,000 people. The A\u0002State campus is centrally located in Jonesboro with the thriving downtown entertainment sector to the west and the growing Hilltop area to the east. Jonesboro provides convenient access to major markets via interstate and four-lane highways. Memphis, TN (1 hour), Little Rock, AR (2 hours), St. Louis, MO (4 hours), and Nashville, TN (4 hours). Additional Considerations: Experience directing theatrical productions. Experience teaching Theatre for non-majors. Experience teaching ballet or other foundational dance techniques. Membership in professional organizations such as SETC, ACDA, or MTEA. Other Teaching Areas of Expertise: Stage Combat, Movement for Actors, Yoga, Non-Western Dance Techniques Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Applicant should present evidence of excellence in teaching, active scholarly and creative work, knowledge of current trends in the field, and artistic leadership in the areas of theatrical dance and choreography. General Days/Hours: Monday through Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM plus additional hours for production(s) on weekdays, weekends and evenings. Other: Application deadline: Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applications for position F00266 must be received online. This position is housed on the Jonesboro campus. Visit https://jobs.astate.edu for detailed information and to apply for the position. Please upload the following: ▪ Cover letter addressing qualifications ▪ Curriculum vitae ▪ Indication of professional dance and/or choreography work, such as a portfolio, performance reel, or documentation of creative work. ▪ Contact information for five professional references Transcripts will be requested by the search committee after initial screening of applicants. For additional information, please contact: DayDay Robinson, Assistant Professor of Theatre. Email: drobinson@astate.edu Minimum Qualifications: ▪ M.F.A. in Theatre, Dance, or a closely related field, or equivalent professional experience. ▪ Demonstrated proficiency in teaching both dance and choreography for theatrical productions. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39924": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 Mo",
      "description": "Department: English and Philosophy\nAssistant Professor 9 Mo | Working Title | Assistant Professor of English | Position # | F00091 | Department | English and Philosophy\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of English Position # F00091 Department English and Philosophy Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/7/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Department of English, Philosophy, and World Languages at Arkansas State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English specializing in Writing Studies, beginning in Fall 27. We welcome candidates working across rhetoric and composition and related fields, including writing pedagogy, literacy studies, professional and technical writing, digital and multimodal writing, writing across the curriculum, multilingual writing, critical pedagogy, and rhetorical theory. These areas are illustrative rather than exhaustive. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in writing, as well as general education composition courses, including Composition I and Composition II, and maintain an active research agenda. The ability to teach creative writing in poetry is preferred, ideally supported by an MFA in poetry. Candidates without this secondary specialization or credential will receive full consideration. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching load of the faculty is normally twelve hours per semester. A reduced teaching load is provided for pre-tenure faculty. Faculty workload also includes research, creative activity, service, and professional development in the best interest of the students and community at large. Arkansas State University provides a number of benefits, including health insurance and retirement. For a complete list, please view: https://www.astate.edu/a/hr/benefits/ Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: We are seeking a dynamic, qualified colleague with the ability to engage students from diverse backgrounds in the study and practice of English writing; evidence and/or potential for successful teaching; evidence and/or potential for an active research program General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date A-State offers an English major, a Writing Studies minor, and a Master’s of English with an emphasis in composition and rhetoric; the Writing Studies minor and Master’s emphasis in composition and rhetoric are growing in both student interest and class offerings. This program features a highly collaborative environment in which faculty work together to create courses and resources to best suit the needs of the diverse and growing student demographic. Teaching load of faculty is normally four courses per semester. Faculty workload also includes research, creative activity and service. Pre-tenure faculty receive a one-class reassignment for research. Arkansas State University serves approximately 14,000 students. The university is committed to quality teaching, including small class sizes, and well-equipped classrooms. It has the largest library in the Arkansas State University System. Jonesboro is an agricultural and industrial city in northeast Arkansas, about 70 miles from Memphis. Qualified candidates should submit electronically: • Letter of application (through online portal) • Curriculum vitae (through online portal) • Research statement (through online portal) • Statement of teaching philosophy (through online portal) • If requested, candidates should arrange to have 3 confidential letters of reference emailed to an address to be provided Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: • Ph.D. in English, Rhetoric and Composition, Writing Studies, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. • Evidence of effective teaching of college-level writing. • Evidence of an active scholarly agenda appropriate to the field of specialization. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience teaching creative writing in poetry, preferably with an MFA in poetry. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39667": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 Mo",
      "description": "Department: Health Sciences and Risk Management\nAssistant Professor 9 Mo | Working Title | Assistant Professor of Health Sciences & Risk Management | Position # | F00496 | Department | Health Sciences and Risk Management\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Health Sciences & Risk Management Position # F00496 Department Health Sciences and Risk Management Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: ASU-Jonesboro Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 10/31/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Arkansas State University Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Health Sciences & Risk Management (tenure-track) to begin in Fall 2027. The position is full-time (9-month) and tenure-track. Duties & Responsibilities: The primary teaching assignment and research focus will be in the Department’s Disaster Preparedness and Emergency Management Program. The ideal candidate will demonstrate potential for an active, high impact emergency management research program. Responsibilities include producing peer-reviewed publications, presenting at professional conferences, and applying for external funding. Additional responsibilities include preparing, developing, and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses across multiple programs in the Department of Health Sciences and Risk Management. Applicants should have the ability to teach a broad range of courses across disciplines such as emergency management, health and/or public administration, policy, research methods, and program development and evaluation. Faculty are expected to maintain regular office hours, mentor undergraduate and graduate students, and participate in course/program assessment. Faculty are also expected to engage in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities that are in the best interest of the students, university, community, and the discipline at large. The ideal candidate will contribute to the development, assessment, and advancement of academic programs, including curriculum development, program assessment, workforce alignment, and engagement with external stakeholders. Arkansas State University is a public research university located in Jonesboro, AR. Arkansas State University is designated by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education as a “Research 2: High Research Spending and Doctorate Production” institution. The Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management has a multidisciplinary and interdisciplinary focus across its programs in Disaster Preparedness & Emergency Management, Dietetics/Nutritional Science, Public Health, Occupational & Environmental Safety & Health, and Health Studies. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: • Strong computer/technology skills required, or possess the ability to easily obtain needed skills. (Microsoft Office, Blackboard Learn and/or Canvas, variety of WEB based programs, etc.) • Strong written and verbal communication skills required. General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Application Instructions Qualified applicants should submit their (1) curriculum vitae, (2) a statement of purpose indicating research interests and teaching philosophy, (3) a writing sample (recent peer-reviewed article or dissertation chapter), and (4) contact information for three academic references, that can speak to your research and teaching, that will be contacted if chosen for an interview. All materials should be submitted online via Taleo, and all items must be submitted to be considered. Application review will begin on the closing date in Taleo and will continue until the position is filled. Questions can be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Amy Hyman, at ahyman@astate.edu. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include a Ph.D. or terminal research degree in an emergency management or closely related discipline. Candidates who are ABD will also be considered, provided they obtain their degree by July 1, 2027. Candidates should have a strong research agenda in the emergency management discipline, or a closely related discipline with an emergency management focus, with evidence of peer-reviewed publications and/or external funding, or the potential to quickly develop a strong research agenda and be immediately successful regarding research and in obtaining external funding. Candidates should also have experience with face-to-face and online teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
    "https://phe.tbe.taleo.net/phe02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ARKASTAT2&cws=56&rid=39991": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor 9 Mo",
      "description": "Department: Health Sciences and Risk Management\nAssistant Professor 9 Mo | Working Title | Assistant Professor of Health Sciences and Risk Management | Position # | F00187 | Department | Health Sciences and Risk Management\nNew Search Login Page Job Details Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Assistant Professor 9 Mo Working Title Assistant Professor of Health Sciences and Risk Management Position # F00187 Department Health Sciences and Risk Management Apply Now Employment Status: Full time (29-40 Hrs) Type of Employment: Faculty # of openings: 1 Location: Telecommute - Jonesboro Campus Proposed Salary Range: Commensurate with Experience Closing: 11/20/26 Please note: All postings close at 12 A.M. CST on the closing date.  This employer participates in E-Verify. Position Summary: The Arkansas State University College of Nursing and Health Professions invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Health Sciences and Risk Management (non-tenure track) to begin in Fall 2027. The position is a full-time (9-month), non-tenure track position. The primary teaching assignment is in the Dietetics and Nutritional Science program in the Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management. Preferred applicants should have the ability to teach across a broad range of disciplines, including courses in nutritional science, health studies public health, and other general healthcare courses within the department. Teaching will be assigned based on the degrees, credentials, and licensures held by candidates, and on the program needs of the programs and department. Duties & Responsibilities: Responsibilities include preparing, developing, and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in the Dietetics and Nutritional Science program, and across multiple programs in the Department of Health Sciences and Risk Management, as credentialed and needed. Applicants should have the ability to teach across a broad range of disciplines, including courses in nutritional science, health studies public health, and other general healthcare courses within the department. Faculty are expected to maintain regular office hours, mentor students, and participate in course/program assessment. Arkansas State University is a public research university located in Jonesboro, AR. Arkansas State University is designated by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education as a “Research 2: High Research Spending and Doctorate Production” institution. The Department of Health Sciences & Risk Management has a multidisciplinary and interdisciplinary focus across its programs in Disaster Preparedness & Emergency Management, Dietetics/Nutritional Science, Public Health, Occupational & Environmental Safety & Health, and Health Studies. Teaching load is 15 hours (5 courses) per semester. Additional responsibilities include maintaining virtual office hours, developing and recording lectures, writing exams, grading, and participating in course/program assessment. The undergraduate program is seeking ACEND accreditation and position may direct the Bachelor of Science in Nutritional Science program per accreditation standards, with workload adjusted accordingly. Application Instructions: Qualified applicants should submit their (1) curriculum vitae, (2) a statement of purpose indicating teaching philosophy, and (3) contact information for three academic references, that can speak to your teaching, that will be contacted if chosen for an interview. All materials should be submitted online via Taleo. Application review will begin on the closing date in Taleo and will continue until the position is filled. Questions can be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Tiffany Sterling, at rsterling@astate.edu . Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Strong computer/technology skills required, or possess the ability to easily obtain the needed skills. (Microsoft, Canvas and/or other Learning Management Systems (LMS), variety of WEB based programs, etc.) Strong written and verbal communication skills required. General Days/Hours: Regular and reliable attendance. Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date This position has been identified as a telecommuting position. The duties are performed during standard work hours of 8am-5pm at a predefined and approved work location. Individuals filling this role must have dedicated workspace that provides privacy and security related to the work being performed. Additionally, individuals must have secure internet access with appropriate upload/download capabilities to perform the duties associated with the position. Individuals in this position will be required to review and acknowledge the Telecommuting Guidelines and Telecommuting Agreement for A-State. Location Requirement: To be considered for this position, candidates must reside in Arkansas or a state that shares a border with Arkansas (Texas, Louisiana, Mississippi, Tennessee, Missouri, or Oklahoma). This residency requirement supports team collaboration, regional knowledge, and occasional in person engagement as needed. Arkansas State University is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer committed to excellence through diversity. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, protected veteran or disabled status, or genetic information. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include a master’s degree in a nutrition/dietetics or healthcare-related discipline. PhD or professional doctorate in a healthcare discipline is strongly preferred. Credentialing as a Registered Dietitian (RD), with three (3) years of professional experience post-credentialing, and ACEND accreditation experience are required. Candidates holding a master’s degree at the time of hire will be appointed at the instructor rank. Candidates holding a PhD, terminal degree, or professional doctorate will be appointed at the assistant professor rank. Potential candidates should possess experience in online teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
    },
