dropping and withdrawing from courses; change of program, major and/or transfer equivalencies) Explains academic policies, procedures, and guidelines to students in order to meet their educational goals Educates students about the value of academic advisement and the importance of the registration process Guides students through college and university level administrative processes Develops and promotes internal communication and resource sharing in order to benefit student success. Encourages interactions with faculty mentors Serves as a liaison for respective colleges at new student orientations and recruitment events Adheres to FERPA and confidentiality of student information Maintains appropriate student records and documents student interactions Utilizes advising and retention technology systems to manage student data May be assigned to support specific academic colleges, programs or student populations May teach a first-year experience course(s) as needed Participates in individual and collaborative professional development and remains current with technology used to provide advising services. Other duties as assigned: Academic advising and all primary responsibilities of this position are supervised by University College. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Excellent computer skills Strong written, oral communication, and interpersonal skills Ability to interact positively with faculty, staff, students, and community members Ability to adapt to and understand university policies and procedures Ability to manage multiple tasks, set priorities, and meet deadlines General Days/Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Occasional Saturday or evening hours Additional hours as requested and/or needed Regular and reliable attendance Other: Please note: all position postings close at 12:00 A.M. CST on the position closing date Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution of higher education Experience in advising or retention programs preferred E-Verify Participation Notice: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/EVerifyParticipationPoster.pdf E-Verify Right to Work: https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RightToWorkPoster%20Eng_Es.pdf Back Apply Now"
